><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20250708113600+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="5ef30d9f-5d0e-4bc0-92ba-aab0f63ce6cf" date="D:20250708113600+10'00'" name="558c5a1e-1793-489f-be2f-032c950f1635" icon="Comment" page="4" rect="306.553040,723.828918,330.553040,747.828918" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal"
>Promote PA as medicine</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>. Use influencers and role&#xD;models in all aspects of life to deliver the message that&#xD;health, wellness and happiness begin at home. That&#xD;PA is the best medicine. That prevention is better&#xD;than cure.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal"
>Lobbying decision-makers</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>.&#xD;Create the toolkits and&#xD;systems so that all members of the GA can lobby&#xD;governments, businesses and non-governmental&#xD;organisations on at all levels to invest in PA to save&#xD;lives, save money and improve society.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal"
>Adapting PA to the individual, community and their&#xD;surroundings</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>. PA must be tailored to the individual,&#xD;their age, gender, socioeconomic and cultural realities&#xD;as well as climatic conditions.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal"
>Leverage the latest tech</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>. Work with the big tech,&#xD;pharma and medical companies and educational&#xD;establishments to build PA into daily life through&#xD;wearable devices, smartphones, the internet and the&#xD;metaverse. Make it easy and fun for people to get into&#xD;PA through gamification, rewards and community&#xD;building.&#xD;</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-10.7pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>► </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;font-style:normal"
>A call for more trials on effectiveness and implementation&#xD;of policies and programs</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>. Most information in&#xD;prevention comes from cohort studies, and there is&#xD;an urgent need for well-designed&#xD;trials for physical&#xD;activity in populations and the healthcare system -&#xD;particularly in respect of underserved minorities.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
